  },
  "articleBody": "When it comes to upgrading your log home's finish, there are some common pitfalls that can lead to big headaches down the road. Let's talk about them so you can avoid them! First off, pressure washing logs is a big no-no for many experts. While it might seem like an easy way to clean, it can actually force a ton of water deep into the wood fibers, which can then get trapped under your new finish. Instead, consider dry methods like corn blasting. Another huge mistake is painting logs. Log homes need to breathe, and traditional paint just doesn't allow for that, often leading to peeling and moisture issues. Always opt for breathable log-specific stains or finishes. Applying a new coating over a failing or incompatible old coating is also a recipe for disaster. The new finish won't adhere properly, and you'll end up with a mess. Always make sure the surface is properly prepped and compatible. And finally, don't rush the drying time! After cleaning or stripping, the logs need to be thoroughly dry before you apply any new finish. Skipping this step can trap moisture underneath, leading to mold and decay. By being aware of these common mistakes, you can ensure your log home finish upgrade looks great and lasts for years. If you're unsure, reach out to HH Remodeling LLC; we serve the greater Denver area and can help you get it right.",
